lies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 21.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.9 to 9.8. December accounts for 24% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 19% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 7. Contract [1], for 14,445 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur due to seasonal demand or budget cycles. High numbers of contracts with the same awardee do not prove misconduct, as multiple needs can justify repeated purchases.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of contracts to see if they align with budget cycles. Review the awardee's history to ensure no single provider is overused. Examine if multiple contracts serve the same purpose to determine if they are redundant or necessary.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["I%2Fq2kb2qySXs%2BnLj3vAg5A%3D%3D","tOIfbOPLZMnmnwcj%2BxbdTg%3D%3D","Sa%2FNbvFeHcJWhbmkna2nXQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}